{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>This is what HaShem spoke, saying</b> — Where did He speak? \"And it shall be sanctified by My glory\" (Exodus 29:43). Do not read \"בִּכְבוֹדִי\" but rather \"בִּמְכֻבָּדָי\" (among those honored by Me). Moses said to Aaron: \"Aaron my brother, I knew that the House would be sanctified through those closest to the Holy One, blessed be He, and I supposed it would be either through me or through you. Now I see that they are greater than me and you.\" This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 10:3), from the midrash of our Rabbis (Leviticus Rabbah 12:2). If so, the meaning of \"and it shall be sanctified by My glory\" would be — that it would be sanctified in the eyes of all the people and among those honored by Me, and they would know that I dwell in it.\n\nAnd Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] also said: \"This is what HaShem spoke, saying\" — HaShem had already told me that He would show His holiness among those close to Him, in the sense of \"You alone have I known from all the families of the earth\" (Amos 3:2). And when I show this holiness in them, then I will be honored before all the people and they will fear Me. And if so, this utterance was not written down, for HaShem had made known to him His ways, that this attribute is before Him.\n\nIn my opinion, according to the plain sense there is no need for any of this, for \"the word of HaShem\" — [means] His decrees, His thoughts, and the matter of His ways. And \"דִּבֶּר\" (spoke) may be said of all these: \"I spoke with my own heart\" (Ecclesiastes 1:16) — I thought this thought. \"And this is the matter that Joshua circumcised\" (Joshua 5:4) — this is the matter. \"Concerning the matter of the silver\" (Genesis 43:18). And likewise \"And let the woman be your master's son's wife, as HaShem spoke\" (Genesis 24:51) — as He decreed. And similar to it: \"In Abiram his firstborn he laid its foundation, and in Segub his youngest he set up its doors, according to the word of HaShem that He spoke through the hand of Joshua son of Nun\" (1 Kings 16:34).\n\nNow Moses said: This occurrence is what HaShem decreed, saying to His heart: \"Among those close to Me I shall be sanctified\" — they shall not profane My holiness — \"and before all the people I shall be honored\" — that they would conduct themselves with honor toward My sanctuary." "And the meaning of <b>And Aaron was silent</b> — that he was crying aloud, and then he fell silent. Or in the sense of \"And let not the daughter of your eye cease\" (Lamentations 2:18)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The word וַיִּדֹּם in comment 1 and the phrase from Lamentations both carry the sense of falling silent; the second proposed meaning references tears that do not cease.", 1 "The Lamentations verse cited (אל תדם) carries the sense of ceasing/stopping; Ramban draws a parallel to show וידם can mean restrained weeping rather than total silence."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:19.662334984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}